bash-project-initializer
========================

A bash script that quickly creates a basic project structure and starter files based off on repositorys main language.

* creates a new project directory
* generates common folders and files
* creates a starter README
* basic .gitignore

Usage
-----

    ./src/main.sh

You will be prompted for:

* Repository name (e.g. `port-repo`)
* Location, the parent directory to create it in (e.g. `/home/foo/git/`)

The script creates the directory and runs 'git init' on it.

Requirements
------------

* yq to handle YAML configuration formats.
